<edge source="middle_east_maritime_con::perceived_shipping_risk" target="china_taiwan_grayzone_pr::investor_risk_perception" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising market and operator assessments of ship attack/seizure risk increase uncertainty and expected costs for firms with cross‑Strait supply chains, prompting investors to mark up political and operational risk for assets exposed to the Taiwan‑China theater.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">middle_east_maritime_con</data>
  <data key="d40">china_taiwan_grayzone_pr</data>
</edge>
<edge source="middle_east_maritime_con::perceived_shipping_risk" target="global_bond_market_shock::nominal_yield_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">A rapid increase in perceived shipping risk raises global risk aversion and triggers flight‑to‑quality flows into sovereign bonds, putting downward pressure on nominal yields in the near term.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">middle_east_maritime_con</data>
  <data key="d40">global_bond_market_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="middle_east_maritime_con::perceived_shipping_risk" target="russia_ukraine_war::alliance_cohesion" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">A sharp rise in perceived risk to merchant shipping from attacks in the Middle East prompts allied navies and governments to coordinate patrols, intelligence-sharing, and diplomatic measures, increasing short-term operational and policy alignment among partners also engaged on Russia–Ukraine issues.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">middle_east_maritime_con</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="middle_east_maritime_con::perceived_shipping_risk" target="us_china_tech_trade_riva::capital_market_liquidity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising shipping risk raises uncertainty and expected loss on cross-border hardware shipments, prompting lenders and investors to mark up risk or pull back financing for capital-intensive AI projects, reducing liquidity available to the sector.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">middle_east_maritime_con</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_trade_riva</data>
</edge>
