</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::energy_supply_gap" target="china_taiwan_grayzone_pr::investor_risk_perception" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Widening energy supply gaps drive higher global energy prices, shipping costs and production disruptions that amplify supply‑chain and inflationary risks for export‑dependent Taiwan, increasing investors' aggregated perception of political‑economic risk in Taiwan‑exposed assets.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">china_taiwan_grayzone_pr</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::energy_supply_gap" target="global_bond_market_shock::nominal_yield_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">A sudden shortfall in gas and oil shipments drives sharp spikes in consumer and producer energy prices, lifting headline inflation and compelling central banks (particularly in Europe) to raise policy rates, which pushes up sovereign nominal yields across maturities.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">global_bond_market_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::energy_supply_gap" target="middle_east_maritime_con::crude_price_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.9</data>
  <data key="d37">A shortfall in available Russian supply tightens global balances and raises benchmark crude prices as markets price the immediate supply deficit and associated risk premia.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">middle_east_maritime_con</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::energy_supply_gap" target="us_china_tech_trade_riva::capital_market_liquidity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Acute fuel and gas shortfalls drive spikes in energy prices and inflationary pressure, prompting faster monetary tightening and risk‑off behavior that reduces the availability and depth of capital markets for AI companies and hardware financing.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_trade_riva</data>
</edge>
