<edge source="global_bond_market_shock::capital_flow_net" target="china_taiwan_grayzone_pr::investor_risk_perception" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">Acute net capital outflows from China/Taiwan assets following a global bond shock raise liquidity and FX concerns and trigger repricing of political and operational risk for regional exposures, directly increasing investor perceptions of cross‑strait investment risk.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_market_shock</data>
  <data key="d40">china_taiwan_grayzone_pr</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_market_shock::capital_flow_net" target="middle_east_maritime_con::maritime_energy_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Net capital outflows from regional markets reduce foreign-exchange liquidity and import financing for energy buyers and charter markets, causing immediate reductions or delays in seaborne crude, product and LNG shipments through Middle East routes.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_market_shock</data>
  <data key="d40">middle_east_maritime_con</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_market_shock::capital_flow_net" target="russia_ukraine_war::resilience_capacity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">A sudden decline in cross‑border capital flows to the conflict region constrains financing for reconstruction contractors and imports of repair equipment and spare parts, slowing restoration and lowering repair capacity.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_market_shock</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_market_shock::capital_flow_net" target="us_china_tech_trade_riva::accel_supply_capacity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Higher net cross‑border capital inflows into hardware‑producing jurisdictions increase available project financing and foreign direct investment for factory build‑out and tooling, lifting accelerator production and deployment capacity over the medium term.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_market_shock</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_trade_riva</data>
</edge>
