  <data key="d37">Spikes in low‑visibility maritime and paramilitary incidents (collisions, seizures, escalatory encounters) produce sudden counterparty losses and margin calls across regional banks and commodity traders, triggering rapid cross‑border liquidity squeezes that transmit stress across sovereign, bank and corporate markets.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
