  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising investor risk perception about a China–Taiwan escalation increases risk premia in oil markets and drives speculative buying of futures and physical stockpiling, pushing benchmark crude prices higher.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
